Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 16:09:12 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] perf(test): share one transactional branch per DB Contract
 mixed suite

The DB Contract lane paid seven transactional branch prepare lifecycles
because accept-path and meeting-ingest each split their transactional
assertions around a dedicated-branch group, creating a second suite
resource that repeated branch creation, migration replay and cleanup.

Move each isolated transactional tail assertion into the file's existing
transactional group, ahead of the dedicated assertions, and drop the extra
withTransactionalDb factory. Seven prepare lifecycles become five. Every
dedicated assertion keeps its own branch, so concurrency, committed
retry/redrive, migration-history and least-privilege proofs stay isolated,
and per-test rollback plus the sentinel observer keep the shared branch
clean between tests.

Lock the shape with an AST-backed topology regression: a routed file with
transactional assertions instantiates exactly one transactional factory,
and all its transactional assertions precede its dedicated ones, so the
suite lease is released before any dedicated branch runs.

Inventory is unchanged: 57 assertions across 9 files, no skips, no timeout
changes.

Forge issue: 5210cc14-ad2c-444a-9ea1-a28a1a68cb64

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
